   "sayWin": [
    "[d113] 💛 You hold Coat button. Breathe. The shaking eases. (−6 trauma)",
    "[d113] 💛 You hold Carpenter's square. Your first solo frame, checked and found true. The nod that followed was the whole ceremony. Measure twice, cut once — it's in your hands now. Your gifts are not mastered — but they are lived-in, and they are with you. The feast was the weapon. (The next feast grants ",
    "[d113] Travel 3 tiles to creek.\n— Moving water —\nThe creek braids around gravel bars. Crawdads flick backward into the shadows of rocks.",
    "[d113] Movement — a bluegill nosing around a shallow bed.",
    "[d113] 👁 It won't leave its bed — that's the whole trick. Pressed, it darts to the center and waits. Reach down and take it, or fish the bed with a worm.",
    "[d113] Travel 2 tiles to creek.\n— Moving water —\nThe creek braids around gravel bars. Crawdads flick backward into the shadows of rocks.",
    "[d113] Travel 2 tiles to forest floor.\n— Under the canopy —\nLeaf litter, birdcall, the smell of rot becoming soil. The woods, being the woods.",
    "[d113] Movement — a waddling porcupine, quills rattling softly.",
    "[d113] 👁 Never grab it barehanded. A bow works clean; hands get quills. Flip it with a long stick if you must.",
    "[d113] Travel 1 tile to forest floor.\n— Under the canopy —\nFallen trunks lie like sleeping animals, furred with moss. The ground gives underfoot — centuries of leaf-mold.",
    "[d113] Travel 3 tiles to grove.\n— Nut trees —\nThe canopy here is a roof built by a thousand architects who never met. Light comes through in coins.",
    "[d113] Travel 2 tiles to creek.\n— Moving water —\nThe water is cold enough to hurt your teeth. Downstream the creek bends out of sight, and you want to follow it. That's the problem with creeks.",
    "[d113] Something moves out there — The Eater.",
    "[d113] You clear the rubble, stone by stone. The path is clear.",
    "[d113] You pocket 3 good throwing stones. (sling ammo)",
    "[d113] Smacking, from the treeline. Rhythmic. Getting closer.",
    "[d113] 👄 It moves.",
    "[d113] Travel 3 tiles to creek.",
    "[d113] It followed you. The Eater is here.",
    "[d113] Travel 2 tiles to Haven.",
    "[d113] The Eater stops at the treeline — pacing, unwilling. The walls end the argument. It's still out there.",
    "[d113] You walk back into Haven. 40 Codex entries. The village is glad to see you.",
    "[d113] Travel 1 tile to grove.",
    "[d113] You also take some vine (crafting material).",
    "[d113] You work the patch with practiced hands: 10× Blackberry (650 kcal). This patch is picked clean — it'll recover in a few days.",
    "[d113] Travel 1 tile to Haven.",
    "[d113] You keep a day's food (650 kcal) — nothing extra for the pantry this time.",
    "[d113] You walk back into Haven. 40 Codex entries. The village is glad to see you.",
    "[d113] You make a Stone knife. flint knapped to an edge, bound with vine. cuts meat, wood, cord.",
    "[d113] You chew the Blackberry deliberately — the way you were taught. Bitter, working. (+8 health)",
    "[d113] You eat Blackberry (650 kcal).",
    "[d113] Your chewing echoes off the trees. Something out there heard. (encounters more likely tomorrow)",
    "[d113] Dawn's an hour off — too late for real sleep. Rest a while instead, or wait for morning.",
    "[d113] The cistern is dry. Haul from a creek (risky water), or put someone on water duty.",
    "[d113] Equipped Stone knife (melee).",
    "[d113] ◈ The realm came apart — no polity answers to Haven now, and Haven is a free fire again. National and global no longer describe this village. The climb starts over.",
    "[d113] ⚠ STARVING: health and energy falling. You went to bed on an empty stomach.",
    "[d113] ⚠ DEHYDRATED: find and treat water today.",
    "[d113] Village meal: +1172 kcal from the communal pantry. (Half ration — they don't trust you yet.)",
    "[d113] ⚠ Haven's pantry is empty. Day 1 of hunger."
   ]
  },
